WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
The reading for this program was provided in part by the Corporation for Public Broadcasting

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.900
and by the financial support of viewers like you.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:13.980
Reach for the speed, reach for the whistle, go where the rail may run.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:22.000
Reach for the word, reach for the story, follow the rainbow sun.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:29.350
To a shining tination, where dreams come true.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:41.600
waiting there missy did you ever wake up on an ordinary morning and wish it wasn't just another

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:49.090
ordinary morning well this morning i did i said to myself self i'm tired of coming home to the same

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:54.990
old front door every day it's time for something new and different adventure and excitement

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.480
I'm going to paint the door a different color.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.060
But what color?

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.160
Not red and green stripes, for sure.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.600
Because of what happened to Henry, the green engine.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:08.880
Remember that?

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:16.100
Once an engine attached to a train was afraid of a few drops of rain.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:22.790
It went into a tunnel and squeaked through its funnel.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.440
It wouldn't come out again.

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:45.940
The engine's name is Henry. His driver and fireman argued with him, but he would not move.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:54.230
The rain will spoil my lovely green paint and red stripes, he said.

00:01:58.430 --> 00:01:59.970
The conductor blew his whistle to leave.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.830
had no more breath and waved his flag till his arms ached. But Henry still stayed in the tunnel

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:12.460
and blew steam at him. I'm not going to spoil my lovely green paint and red stripes for you.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:20.000
Then along came Sir Topham Hatt, the man in charge of all the engines on the island of Sodor.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:29.960
We will pull you out, said Sir Topham Hatt.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.470
Henry only blew steam at him.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.660
Everyone pulled except Sir Topham Hatt,

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.100
because, he said, my doctor has forbidden me to pull.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:47.090
But still, Henry stayed in the tunnel.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:51.630
Then they tried pushing from the other end.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:55.440
Sir Topham Hatt said, one, two, three, push!

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:05.900
But he didn't help. My doctor has forbidden me to push, he said.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:12.000
They pushed and pushed and pushed. But still, Henry stayed in the tunnel.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:20.260
At last, Thomas came along. The conductor waved his red flag and stopped him.

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:23.030
Everyone argued with Henry.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:25.650
Look, it has stopped raining, they said.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.680
Yes, but it will begin again soon, said Henry.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:32.890
And what would become of my green paint with red stripes then?

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:43.310
Thomas pushed and puffed and pushed as hard as ever he could.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.500
Still, Henry stayed in the tunnel.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.960
Eventually, even Sir Topham Hatt gave...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.860
We shall take away your rails, he said, and leave you here until you're ready to come out of the tunnel.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:16.580
They took up the old rails and built a wall in front of Henry so that other engines wouldn't bump into him.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:39.240
All Henry could do was to watch the trains rushing through the other tunnel.

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:48.650
He was very sad because he thought no one would ever see his lovely green paint with red stripes again.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:53.020
As time went on, Edward and Gordon would often pass by.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:56.400
Edward would say,

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:57.860
Beep, beep, hello.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:05.160
And Gordon would say, serves you right.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:08.720
Poor Henry had no steam to answer.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.720
His fire had gone out.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:17.520
Soot and dirt from the tunnel had spoiled his lovely green paint and red stripes anyway.

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:25.610
How long do you think Henry will stay in the tunnel before he overcomes his fear of the rain and decides to journey out again?

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:29.760
I don't know.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:37.340
something's wrong here i usually like green reminds me of springtime it's the color of leaves

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:45.170
and grass but this particular green is the color of fish not that i have anything against fish some

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:51.480
of my best friends are fish it's just that after what happened to henry did i ever tell you about

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:59.970
henry and the fish on starry nights when the moon is full and the air still you can

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.400
hear the sounds of faraway ships and distant laughter. They echo over the hills and through

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:12.160
the valley, down calm canals and sleepy inlets. Every engine knows that these are the sounds

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:22.320
that say the harbor is hard at work at the big station by the sea. One night, a special load of

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:27.310
